{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l collab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm*.md docs/design/{yin.vm.engine,yin.vm.debruijn.register,yang.wasm,yin.vm.rust-kernel}.md; rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} '\"' docs/design/{yin.vm.engine,yin.vm.debruijn.register,yang.wasm}.md collab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm*.md\"","aggregated_output":"     495 collab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md\n     417 collab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md\n    1296 docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md\n    1735 docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md\n     556 docs/design/yang.wasm.md\n    1338 docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md\n    5837 total\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:1:# yin.vm.conformance-kit: the shared R4 execution conformance kit\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:26:## 1. Scope and authorities\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:52:## 2. Exported fixtures and execution lanes\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:129:## 3. Encoding and hash determinism\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:200:## 4. Deterministic traversal prerequisite\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:253:## 5. W0 transport, profile and toolchain gates\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:318:## 6. Per-slice differential acceptance\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:320:### W1 — pure register execution and body dispatch\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:338:### W2 — continuations and restore\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:358:### W3 — streams, shared scheduler and FFI\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:394:### W4 — attach, modules and lifetime correctness\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:424:### W5 — lane completion and release gate\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:447:### W6 — measured optimization, after correctness\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:466:## 7. Rust and LLVM acceptance retained\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md:490:## 8. Open items\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:1:# yang.wasm: lowering register images to WebAssembly modules\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:32:## Authorities\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:48:## 1. Pipeline position, decision and source precedence\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:123:### 1.1 Rust-kernel authority, scope and explicit reconciliations\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:156:## 2. Emitted module contract and linear-memory layout\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:158:### 2.1 Values in emitted code: i32 ValueRef locals\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:190:### 2.2 Private linear-memory layout\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:230:### 2.3 Module imports, exports and deterministic emission\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:255:## 3. Code generation strategy and all 23 opcode lowerings\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:257:### 3.1 Choice among the alternatives\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:288:### 3.1.1 LLVM sibling and shared equivalence law\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:300:### 3.2 Structuring algorithm\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:308:### 3.3 All 23 opcode lowerings\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:342:### 3.4 Exact host-function effect completion\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:364:### 3.5 Boundary continuation payload and internal continuation call\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:404:## 4. Target interface specification: Import ABI `yin.vm.engine.host.v1`\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:426:## 5. Per-image-row compilation, relocation, and artifact-cache law\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:487:## 6. Compiler toolchain, optimization axis (W6), non-goals, and risks\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:489:### 6.1 Toolchain and W0–W6 lowering gates\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:501:### 6.2 Lowering non-goals and risks\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:520:## Reference conventions\ndocs/design/yang.wasm.md:545:## Open items\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:1:# yin.vm.register-wasm: the WebAssembly execution host for register images\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:33:## Authorities\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:48:## 1. Register machine state and the register instance of the synchronization barrier\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:62:### 1.1 The eight materialized register fields and the synchronization barrier instance\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:93:### 1.2 Dense register shadow, sparse saved frames, and register GC roots\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:119:## 2. Sparse continuation materialization, `register-restore`, and layout transport\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:121:### 2.1 Materialization and capture-time metadata\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:144:### 2.2 `register-restore` algorithm and failure ordering\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:169:### 2.3 Cross-runtime continuation transport and layout compatibility\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:190:### 2.4 Register wait-entry validation scope\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:205:## 3. Register module attachment, `spawn-module`, and artifact cache\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:235:## 4. Register-specific W0–W6 implementation slices and acceptance gates\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:237:### 4.1 Register test harness and corpora\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:250:### 4.2 W0 — Register admission, codec, and synchronization gates\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:262:### 4.3 W1 — Pure register execution and body dispatch\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:287:### 4.4 W2 — Sparse continuations and `register-restore`\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:311:### 4.5 W3 — Streams, shared scheduler, and FFI on register images\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:335:### 4.6 W4 — Runtime `attach-image`, modules, and lifetime correctness\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:358:### 4.7 W5 — Register lane completion and release gate\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:367:### 4.8 W6 — Measured optimization and register non-goals\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:385:## 5. Register-specific risks, Reference conventions, and Open items\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:402:### Reference conventions\ncollab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.register-wasm.md:411:### Open items\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1:# yin.vm de Bruijn register VM\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:73:## 1. Objective and invariants\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:150:### 1.1 Identity and sharing\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:183:## 2. Compilation topology and stream contract\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:231:### 2.1 The shared artifact: resolved tuples\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:290:### 2.2 Relation to B2 as implemented\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:329:## 3. Register dimension\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:384:## 4. Resolved-tuples-to-register lowering\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:386:### 4.1 Input and validation\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:408:### 4.2 Register classes\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:430:### 4.3 Determinism\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:444:### 4.4 Instruction mapping\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:556:### 4.5 Live sets at continuation boundaries\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:665:### 4.6 R2 lowering rules\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:711:## 5. Execution boundary\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:729:### 5.1 Continuation transport across VM models\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:776:### 5.2 R2 effect and suspension contract\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:794:#### 5.2.1 Effect dispatch\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:839:#### 5.2.2 Sparse continuation representation\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:904:#### 5.2.3 Engine restoration and wait entries\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:965:## 6. Implementation phases\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:970:### R0: contract and corpus\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:988:### R1: register dimension and lowerer\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1006:### R2: effects and stream forms\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1066:### R3: benchmark report\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1080:### R4: register kernel\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1110:### R5: linker integration over dao.stream\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1126:## 7. Non-goals and protected surfaces\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1145:## 8. Risks and decisions\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1198:## 9. End condition\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1211:## 10. Wasm execution instance (2026-10-19, design only)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1260:### 10.1 Register machine state and the register instance of the synchronization barrier\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1274:#### 10.1.1 The eight materialized register fields and the synchronization barrier instance\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1305:#### 10.1.2 Dense register shadow, sparse saved frames, and register GC roots\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1329:### 10.2 Sparse continuation materialization, `register-restore`, and layout transport\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1331:#### 10.2.1 Materialization and capture-time metadata\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1351:#### 10.2.2 `register-restore` algorithm and failure ordering\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1376:#### 10.2.3 Cross-runtime continuation transport and layout compatibility\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1397:#### 10.2.4 Register wait-entry validation scope\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1410:### 10.3 Register module attachment, `spawn-module`, and artifact cache\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1438:### 10.4 Register conformance fixture schema (K0/W0)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1469:### 10.5 Register-specific W0–W6 implementation slices and acceptance gates\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1479:#### 10.5.1 W0 — Register admission, codec, and eight-field synchronization gates\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1495:#### 10.5.2 W1 — Pure register execution and body dispatch\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1522:#### 10.5.3 W2 — Continuations and `register-restore`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1549:#### 10.5.4 W3 — Streams, shared scheduler, and FFI\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1599:#### 10.5.5 W4 — Attach, modules, and lifetime correctness\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1638:#### 10.5.6 W5 — Lane completion and release gate\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1667:#### 10.5.7 W6 — Measured optimization and register non-goals\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1697:#### 10.5.8 Rust K1–K5 and LLVM acceptance retained\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1712:### 10.6 Register-specific risks, reference conventions, and open items\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:1:# yin.vm engine: the VM seam\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:27:## 1. What the engine owns\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:57:### 1.1 Names and the program store (Rule R)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:137:## 2. What a VM supplies\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:141:### 2.1 The restore function\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:168:### 2.2 The park-entry builder\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:187:## 3. The entry key contract\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:230:## 4. The FFI two-step\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:260:## 5. Glue that is pure duplication\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:280:## 6. Why not a protocol\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:316:## 7. Proposed engine edits (B4's file box)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:349:## 8. Findings outside B4's scope\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:363:## Extension (2026-10-19, design only): the engine execution host for guest machines\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:405:### E.1 The machine-state-as-data boundary and synchronization protocol\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:456:### E.2 The value arena, handle discipline, and three encoding domains\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:458:#### E.2.1 Task-owned value arena, `i32` handles, and the native `handle↔Value` facade\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:526:#### E.2.2 Three encoding domains and mandatory native hashing\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:597:#### E.2.3 Arena collection, GC root discipline, and snapshot isolation\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:621:### E.3 Service protocol: `yin.vm.engine.host.v1`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:641:#### E.3.1 Offsets and ownership\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:684:#### E.3.2 Transport status values, execution statuses, and once-only response delivery\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:716:#### E.3.3 Plain-data TLV encoding, canonical ordering, and Float64/NaN rules\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:786:#### E.3.4 Message envelope, task-local references, and required operations\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:830:### E.4 The embedder seam, single-engine-port rule, and deterministic traversal\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:832:#### E.4.1 Host responsibilities, embedder targets, and `IVM` `step`/`run` contract\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:890:#### E.4.2 Single-engine-port rule, fault containment, and Rust-kernel reconciliations\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:942:#### E.4.3 Deterministic service traversal prerequisite\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:1001:#### E.4.4 Stream, park, custody-gate, FFI two-step, and `spawn-module` host rules\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:1045:### E.5 Conformance method, guest-agnostic acceptance gates, toolchain pins, non-goals, risks, and open items\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:1054:#### E.5.1 Oracle export, differential execution lanes, and trace comparison method\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:1137:#### E.5.2 Cross-embedder encoding, hash, and traversal determinism gates\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:1174:#### E.5.3 W0 baseline toolchain pins, feature probes, and transport/snapshot gates\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:1256:#### E.5.4 Guest-agnostic non-goals and risks\ndocs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:1277:#### E.5.5 Reference conventions and open items\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
