{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re,difflib\nlive='\\\\n'.join(Path('docs/design/'+n+'.md').read_text() for n in ['yin.vm.engine','yin.vm.debruijn.register','yang.wasm'])\ndef norm(t):\n t=re.sub(r'\\\\[([\"'^]]+)'\"\\\\]\\\\([\"'^)]+'\"\\\\)',r'\\\\1',t)\n t=re.sub(r'§\\\\S+','',t)\n return re.sub(r'\\\\s+',' ',t.replace('\"'`'\"','').replace('*','').replace('’',\\\"'\\\").replace('“','\\\"').replace('”','\\\"')).lower()\n# Find sentences whose core words need manual mapping, skipping links/headings/provenance.\nnlive=norm(live)\nfor name in ['conformance-kit','register-wasm']:\n s=Path('collab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.'+name+'.md').read_text()\n missing=[]\n for p in s.split('\\\\n\\\\n'):\n  if p.startswith(('#','|')):continue\n  for sentence in re.split(r'(?<=[.\"'!?])'\"\\\\s+',p):\n   n=norm(sentence)\n   if len(n)>100 and n not in nlive:\n    ratio=difflib.SequenceMatcher(None,n,nlive,autojunk=False).find_longest_match().size/len(n)\n    if ratio<.60: missing.append((s[:s.index(sentence[:30])].count('\\\\n')+1 if sentence[:30] in s else '?',round(ratio,2),n[:260]))\n print(name,'candidate changed sentences (manual review, not findings):')\n for row in missing: print(row)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.wasm.md | sed -n '404,423p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md | sed -n '1090,1121p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md | sed -n '1460,1470p'; git status --short -- docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md docs/design/yang.wasm.md docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.wasm.md | sed -n '404,423p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md | sed -n '1090,1121p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md | sed -n '1460,1470p'; git status --short -- docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md docs/design/yang.wasm.md docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md\"","aggregated_output":"   404\t## 4. Target interface specification: Import ABI `yin.vm.engine.host.v1`\n   405\t\n   406\t*(Owner amendment note, 2026-10-19: By explicit owner ruling, the service import ABI is named\n   407\t`yin.vm.engine.host.v1` — renamed from `yin.register.host.v1` in r5 §4.1.1 — and its canonical\n   408\tprotocol tables live in [`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3. This section specifies the\n   409\tcompiler's target-interface binding and references those tables rather than duplicating them.)*\n   410\t\n   411\tEmitted WebAssembly modules target the guest-agnostic engine service protocol\n   412\t**`yin.vm.engine.host.v1`** defined in [`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3 (r5 §4.1.1):\n   413\t\n   414\t1. **Module import bindings ([`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3):** The shared runtime module imports `memory` (one wasm32, non-shared memory), `functions` (one original function table), and **`exchange(control_ptr: i32) -> i32`** from module name `yin.vm.engine.host.v1`. Generated component modules import the same `memory`/`functions` and the service entry as needed, plus declared immutable `i32` base-offset words. No import or export passes a JS value, `externref`, Rust pointer, string object, multi-value result, or `i64` through a host-call signature.\n   415\t2. **Control-block layout and buffer ownership ([`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3.1):** Emitted service thunks address ABI control at bytes `0–255` (`control_ptr = 0` in v1, magic `0x31524e59` at `+0`, major `1` at `+4`, minor `0` at `+8`, header length `64` at `+12`, request pointer/length at `+16`/`+20`, response pointer/capacity at `+24`/`+28`, response written length at `+32`, required length at `+36`, sequence low/high at `+40`/`+44`, transport status at `+48`, flags at `+52`, reserved zero at `+56`/`+60`; initial request region `[256, 32768)`, response region `[32768, 65536)`, task allocation starting at `65536`). Guest allocation/growth occurs between `exchange` calls, never inside `exchange`.\n   416\t3. **Transport statuses, execution statuses, and `fetch-response` ([`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3.2):** Emitted service thunks handle transport return statuses `0 COMPLETE`, `1 NEED_SPACE`, `2 BAD_MESSAGE`, `3 ABI_MISMATCH`, and `4 RESOURCE_LIMIT`. On `NEED_SPACE`, the guest thunk resizes the response buffer to the required byte length at `+36` and issues a `fetch-response` for the same sequence number without re-executing or re-sending the semantic transition. Decoded responses carry the private scheduling status (`TRANSFER`, `HOST_SERVICE`, `YIELDED`, `BLOCKED`, `PARKED`, `HALTED`, `ERROR`).\n   417\t4. **TLV framing, expanded-canonical-bytes ordering, and Float64/NaN encoding ([`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3.3):** All request/response payloads and constant/value definitions emitted or decoded by the runtime module obey the single outer framing rule (`u8 tag | u32 payload-byte-length (LE) | payload` for tags `0`–`13`, with no inner counts), sort map keys and set elements by recursively expanded canonical value bytes before tag-`13` handle compression, and encode every Float64 NaN as `0x7ff8000000000000` (`00 00 00 00 00 00 f8 7f` LE).\n   418\t5. **Message envelope, register snapshot fields, and compiled vs. service division ([`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3.4, [`yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`](./yin.vm.debruijn.register.md) §10.1):** Each service request carries the materialized register execution snapshot (`pc`/`registers`/`frames`/`K`/`store-of`/`value`/`halted`/`blocked` plus layout generation) before any service that can collect or park. External continuation export resolves tag-`13` arena references to the payload values in §3.5 or refuses. Pure body control, register moves, and guest closure calls stay compiled in the emitted wasm module; the host service is never allowed to “run the remaining program” to manufacture the expected trace.\n   419\t\n   420\tThe host-side implementation of `yin.vm.engine.host.v1`, the **single-engine-port rule**, and the\n   421\t“one transition implementation, two dispatchers” rule are specified in\n   422\t[`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.4.1 and §E.4.2.\n   423\t\n  1090\tprimitive registry, origin and counter setup. From W1 onward, compile each\n  1091\timage once and run those identical wasm bytes under **Node and Wasmtime**,\n  1092\teach against interpreted register after every guest instruction and scheduler\n  1093\tevent; Wasmer must also pass the complete suite by W5. Compare serialized ABI\n  1094\ttraffic as well as full semantic traces; also compare semantic execution where\n  1095\tthe existing A→R fragment permits it.\n  1096\t\n  1097\tUse `test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc` **programs and literal goldens**:\n  1098\tproject AST to A, assert the literal vector/address, derive R, validate R/live\n  1099\tsets, compile and instantiate wasm. These goldens specify syntax/address, not\n  1100\ta runnable environment or expected final value for every entry. Supply\n  1101\tdeterministic `f`/`g`/`h`/`k`/`x`/`y`/`c`/`loop` bindings, stream fixtures,\n  1102\tand genuine parked targets for resume cases; otherwise compare the same\n  1103\tqualified refusal. Execute both conditional arms where applicable. Do not\n  1104\tsilently skip resume/terminal/closure cases or relabel unsupported cases as\n  1105\tsuccesses.\n  1106\t\n  1107\tUse all fixtures/assertions of `test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc`,\n  1108\tincluding hand images, B0/B2 parity, stream scripts, continuation corruption,\n  1109\tand IVM behavior. B0 normalization is suitable for final cross-model values\n  1110\tbut is insufficient for this backend: additionally compare raw register\n  1111\tpayload shapes, stores/module-stores, `pc`, frame order, `K`, counter, flags,\n  1112\twait/ready/parked entries and emitted request traces. Compare resources by\n  1113\tauthenticated logical identity/cursor progress and stream emissions, not by\n  1114\thost object address. With identical secrets and inputs,\n  1115\thash/owner/seal/profile/address strings, guest-visible ids and slice ordering\n  1116\tmust be bit-identical. Compare canonical expanded observable-state encodings,\n  1117\tnot pointer layouts; private arena numbers may be renamed only where they\n  1118\tcannot affect key ordering, id minting or guest state. Across independent\n  1119\ttasks use the same explicit owner inputs; never erase owner checks. Test\n  1120\tprimitive implementations and scripted transports exist in both native and\n  1121\tCLJS compositions with the same declared profiles; a JS function fixture must\n  1460\t- tail-site fixtures for every row of the Rust design's §7.3 call-outcome table (including a tail primitive value and a tail primitive effect returning into a caller in another body, and halting with `K` empty; `docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:833–918`),\n  1461\t- a wide-body fixture whose register count exceeds `65,535`,\n  1462\t- `:host-limit` refusal fixtures, and\n  1463\t- the million-iteration tail fixtures.\n  1464\t\n  1465\tRequired repository corpora for register-wasm and Rust K0–K5:\n  1466\t- `test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc` **programs and literal goldens**: project AST to `A`, assert the literal vector/address, derive `R`, validate `R`/live sets, compile and instantiate wasm. These goldens specify syntax/address, not a runnable environment or expected final value for every entry. Supply deterministic `f`/`g`/`h`/`k`/`x`/`y`/`c`/`loop` bindings, stream fixtures, and genuine parked targets for resume cases; otherwise compare the same qualified refusal. Execute both conditional arms where applicable. Do not silently skip resume/terminal/closure cases or relabel unsupported cases as successes.\n  1467\t- All fixtures and assertions of `test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc` (plus `test/yin/vm/debruijn_code_test.cljc` and `test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code_test.cljc`), including hand images, B0/B2 parity, stream scripts, continuation corruption, and `IVM` behavior. Beyond B0 normalization, compare raw register payload shapes, `store`/`module-stores`, `pc`, frame order, `K`, counter, flags, `wait-set`/`ready-queue`/`parked` entries, and emitted request traces.\n  1468\t\n  1469\t### 10.5 Register-specific W0–W6 implementation slices and acceptance gates\n  1470\t\n M docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md\n M docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md\n?? docs/design/yang.wasm.md\n?? docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re,difflib\nlive='\\\\n'.join(Path('docs/design/'+n+'.md').read_text() for n in ['yin.vm.engine','yin.vm.debruijn.register','yang.wasm'])\ndef norm(t):\n t=re.sub(r'\\\\[([\"'^]]+)'\"\\\\]\\\\([\"'^)]+'\"\\\\)',r'\\\\1',t)\n t=re.sub(r'§\\\\S+','',t)\n return re.sub(r'\\\\s+',' ',t.replace('\"'`'\"','').replace('*','').replace('’',\\\"'\\\").replace('“','\\\"').replace('”','\\\"')).lower()\n# Find sentences whose core words need manual mapping, skipping links/headings/provenance.\nnlive=norm(live)\nfor name in ['conformance-kit','register-wasm']:\n s=Path('collab/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.'+name+'.md').read_text()\n missing=[]\n for p in s.split('\\\\n\\\\n'):\n  if p.startswith(('#','|')):continue\n  for sentence in re.split(r'(?<=[.\"'!?])'\"\\\\s+',p):\n   n=norm(sentence)\n   if len(n)>100 and n not in nlive:\n    ratio=difflib.SequenceMatcher(None,n,nlive,autojunk=False).find_longest_match().size/len(n)\n    if ratio<.60: missing.append((s[:s.index(sentence[:30])].count('\\\\n')+1 if sentence[:30] in s else '?',round(ratio,2),n[:260]))\n print(name,'candidate changed sentences (manual review, not findings):')\n for row in missing: print(row)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 18, in <module>\nconformance-kit candidate changed sentences (manual review, not findings):\n(14, 0.14, 'decomposition: updated cross-references for the owner-directed decomposition into yin.vm.engine.md ( guest-agnostic execution host and service protocol), yang.wasm.md (register-image-to-webassembly lowering), and yin.vm.register-wasm.md (register-machine host ')\n(20, 0.42, 'owner ruling (2026-10-19): by explicit owner ruling, the service import abi is renamed yin.register.host.v1 → yin.vm.engine.host.v1 and its canonical protocol tables live in yin.vm.engine.md ')\n(28, 0.35, 'this is the single k0/w0 shared deliverable of yin.vm.rust-kernel.md, yin.vm.engine.md ( yang.wasm.md, and yin.vm.register-wasm.md.')\n(38, 0.27, 'the register, semantic, linker and engine authorities listed in yin.vm.engine.md ( yang.wasm.md, and yin.vm.register-wasm.md govern the reference behavior.')\n(42, 0.37, \"rust k0's fixture description is at docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md:1185–1199; its equivalence law is at :805–831.\")\n(44, 0.13, 'guest-agnostic host and yin.vm.engine.host.v1 protocol § references below cite yin.vm.engine.md ( lowering-lane § references cite yang.wasm.md; register-instance § references cite yin.vm.register-wasm.md; rust-design sections are explicitly qualified.')\n(54, 0.22, 'the kit exports, per corpus program: the image as canonical data, r, the b0-normalized result or error, and the format-level trace r4 produces (payload at every boundary, k depth, saved pairs).')\n(56, 0.23, 'plus: refusal fixtures for all fourteen validator rules with rule keywords, the descriptor hash, scalar-encoding vectors, diagnostic message fixtures, atomicity fixtures (a refused step leaves the state equal), tail-site fixtures for every row of the 7.3 table')\n(70, 0.24, 'consume and extend its canonical images, r, b0-normalized results/errors, boundary payloads/k depth/saved pairs, descriptor/scalar vectors, ordered validator refusals/messages and refused-step atomicity fixtures.')\n(187, 0.21, \"the private yin.vm.engine.host.v1 abi's complete tag table, control offsets, status values and message schema are specified in yin.vm.engine.md (r5 target binding in yang.wasm.md \")\n(210, 0.48, 'for currently unordered traversal sites use a pure order key: for ordinary machine values, the fully expanded canonical yin.vm.engine.host.v1 abi value bytes defined in yin.vm.engine.md (r5 for trusted values, their non-minting structural descriptors.')\n(248, 0.53, 'version the kit after that stabilization and retain the original goldens/history, as specified in yin.vm.engine.md and yang.wasm.md rust-authority reconciliation; do not silently choose rust map order or normalize away changed guest-visible ids.')\n(255, 0.43, \"deliver/extend k0's single exported fixture kit and its cljs, rust-interpreter and wasm adapters, the core-profile feature probe, pinned assembler/validator, abi codec/schema and operation-by-operation conformance fixtures.\")\n(291, 0.42, 'freeze the map/memory authority protocol and its byte-message equivalents, including external assoc/snapshot replacement, old-state replay and preservation of unknown engine extension keys; do not defer that contract to performance tuning.')\n(346, 0.57, 'add nested non-tail capture then abortive invocation, multi-shot capture, tail return-result, live closure versus live primitive distinctions under machine-data?, host-function/error resume refusal, error-shaped data success, dead-slot nil restoration, snapsho')\n(354, 0.56, 'add an unowned wrong-arity continuation case proving foreign-value precedes continuation-arity, and an owned wrong-arity/foreign-format case proving arity precedes format.')\n(381, 0.59, 'scope wait-entry-defect to its four shapes; use payload plus owning-shape checks for observe/link/install.')\n(492, 0.22, \"the frozen r5 ambiguities recorded in yin.vm.engine.md yang.wasm.md's, and yin.vm.register-wasm.md's open items remain open here as well, including the w0 complete→need_space→fetch-response notation.\")\n(494, 0.13, 'the source requirements above are retained without resolving those details or changing the transport state machine.')\n  File \"/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Library/Frameworks/Python3.framework/Versions/3.9/lib/python3.9/difflib.py\", line 417, in find_longest_match\n    k = newj2len[j] = j2lenget(j-1, 0) + 1\nKeyboardInterrupt\n","exit_code":130,"status":"failed"}}
