{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff -- docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md | head -150; git diff -- docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md | head -50'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md b/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md\nindex db6060e34..815c06d85 100644\n--- a/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md\n+++ b/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md\n@@ -4,6 +4,19 @@ Status: contract of the existing `yin.vm.engine` namespace as of 2026-09-22,\n plus three additive engine edits proposed for B4 of\n `yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md`. No protocol is introduced; see section 6.\n \n+2026-10-19 correction note: In the 2026-09-22 body below (§1.1, §2.1, §3),\n+historical `:store-updates` / `{:rule :store-update-key}` wording has been\n+corrected to match current `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc`: ready entries\n+carry `:resource-updates` merged into private `:resources`, refusing\n+non-keyword keys with `{:rule :resource-update-key}`.\n+\n+2026-10-19 design extension: Added\n+[`## Extension (2026-10-19, design only): the engine execution host for guest machines`](#extension-2026-10-19-design-only-the-engine-execution-host-for-guest-machines)\n+below (§E.1–§E.5), holding the guest-agnostic host execution specification\n+and the `yin.vm.engine.host.v1` service ABI (renamed from\n+`yin.register.host.v1` by owner ruling on 2026-10-19). Sections 1–8 remain\n+authoritative for landed engine behavior.\n+\n `yin.vm.engine` is the shared scheduler for every Yin VM: the dispatch loop,\n wait-set polling, ready-queue resumption, park and resume records, and the\n stream-effect handlers. It is VM-agnostic because every place it needs to\n@@ -58,9 +71,11 @@ stack, and register VMs, and all four definition transitions write\n through it, and none of those transitions resolves its operator. A\n program therefore cannot redirect a definition through any binding.\n \n-`resume-from-run-queue` asserts that a ready entry's `:store-updates`\n-carries only keyword keys, the ones the engine mints, and refuses any\n-other key with `{:rule :store-update-key}`.\n+`resume-from-run-queue` asserts that a ready entry's `:resource-updates`\n+(historically written `:store-updates` in the 2026-09-22 draft; corrected\n+2026-10-19) carries only keyword keys, the ones the engine mints, merges\n+them into private `:resources`, and refuses any other key with\n+`{:rule :resource-update-key}` (historically `{:rule :store-update-key}`).\n \n Every other store write the audit detects is state construction and\n sits on an allowlist, enforced by the store-write audit\n@@ -128,9 +143,10 @@ Exactly one VM-level function and one instruction-site builder shape.\n     restore : base entry val -> state\n \n `base` is the VM state after the engine has done its part: the ready entry\n-popped, `:store-updates` merged, `:blocked?` and `:halted?` cleared (from\n-`resume-from-run-queue`, which first asserts keyword keys, section\n-1.1), or the parked record removed (from\n+popped, `:resource-updates` merged into `:resources` (historically written\n+`:store-updates` in the 2026-09-22 draft; corrected 2026-10-19), `:blocked?`\n+and `:halted?` cleared (from `resume-from-run-queue`, which first asserts\n+keyword keys, section 1.1), or the parked record removed (from\n `resume-continuation`). `entry` is the wait, ready, or parked record. `val`\n is the value the parked instruction receives: the woken stream value, or the\n resume operand.\n@@ -176,9 +192,12 @@ parked entry is the union of two disjoint key sets.\n Engine-owned keys, read or written by the engine and `dao.stream.waitset`:\n \n     :reason  :stream-id  :cursor-ref  :datom\n-    :value  :status  :store-updates  :cursor\n+    :value  :status  :resource-updates  :cursor\n     :type  :id                           (parked records only)\n \n+*(2026-10-19 correction: `:resource-updates` replaces the 2026-09-22 draft's\n+`:store-updates` to match `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc`.)*\n+\n `:stream` may appear on a woken entry transiently and is dropped before the\n entry reaches the ready queue.\n \n@@ -338,3 +357,940 @@ and the inline round from `ast_walker.cljc`) and is the owner's call.\n - `ready-for-ingress?` speaks the named register vocabulary (section 1).\n - The semantic VM's private `response-wait-entry` becomes redundant with\n   edit 3 above.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Extension (2026-10-19, design only): the engine execution host for guest machines\n+\n+Status: design, owner-authorized planning; not implemented. The existing\n+document body (§1–§8 above) remains authoritative for landed `yin.vm.engine`\n+behavior.\n+\n+Consensus provenance (2026-10-18): gpt-6-astra, author; gemini-4-argon,\n+reviewer; five review rounds, APPROVE on r5. Author thread:\n+`01a14f30-ca56-7530-bb93-3a870eca7a7b`; reviewer thread:\n+`f365ef1d-caa2-4379-8e96-51e64ca36af8`. It does not report an\n+implementation or runtime acceptance result.\n+\n+Owner amendment, decomposition, and fold notes (2026-10-19):\n+1. **Owner ruling (2026-10-19, ABI naming and host home)**: The\n+   host-independent execution content lives in `yin.vm.engine` (\"since its\n+   `yin.vm.engine` then it should be `yin.vm.engine.host.v1`\"), and the\n+   service ABI is renamed `yin.register.host.v1` → `yin.vm.engine.host.v1`.\n+2. **Owner ruling (2026-10-19, document fold)**: By explicit owner ruling,\n+   `docs/design/yin.vm.register-wasm.md` and\n+   `docs/design/yin.vm.conformance-kit.md` are retired and folded into the\n+   existing architecture documents:\n+   - This extension (`§E.1–§E.5`) holds the guest-agnostic execution-host\n+     contract, the canonical `yin.vm.engine.host.v1` service protocol tables,\n+     and the **conformance method** (`§E.5`, folded from\n+     `yin.vm.conformance-kit.md` `§1–§5`, `§8`).\n+   - [`yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`](./yin.vm.debruijn.register.md) `§10`\n+     holds the register machine's specific wasm execution instance (folded from\n+     `yin.vm.register-wasm.md` `§1–§5`) together with the register fixture\n+     schema and register W0–W6 / Rust K1–K5 lane gates (folded from\n+     `yin.vm.conformance-kit.md` `§2`, `§6`, `§7`).\n+   - [`yang.wasm.md`](./yang.wasm.md) holds register-image-to-WebAssembly\n+     lowering and the 23 opcode lowerings. Normative content is otherwise\n+     frozen.\n+\n+Authorities and companion specifications:\n+- [datom.world.md](./datom.world.md): foundational axioms and invariants.\n+- [yin.vm.semantic.md](./yin.vm.semantic.md): A identity and semantic execution.\n+- [yin.vm.debruijn.register.md](./yin.vm.debruijn.register.md): register contract, live sets, sparse continuations, and (§10) the register wasm execution instance, register fixture schema, and register W0–W6 / Rust K1–K5 conformance gates.\n+- [yin.vm.linker.md](./yin.vm.linker.md): admission, offset tables and module transport.\n+- [yin.vm.rust-kernel.md](./yin.vm.rust-kernel.md): shared Rust crates, Value ownership, transition reuse and LLVM relationship.\n+- [yang.wasm.md](./yang.wasm.md): lowering register images to WebAssembly modules, targeting `yin.vm.engine.host.v1`.\n+\n+### E.1 The machine-state-as-data boundary and synchronization protocol\n+\n+A guest machine's execution state must materialize as plain host-readable\n+data at every service boundary; the host never reaches into guest-private\n+storage. Each task owns one imported, non-shared wasm32 linear-memory arena\n+as a private execution cache; separate tasks receive separate arenas even\n+when compiled Module objects are cached. A supplied `coremem` can implement\n+the same interface only with task isolation and allocation ownership; shared\n+mutable guest state is not introduced.\n+\n+The public CLJS VM remains a persistent record with ordinary map keys, not a\n+token that requires callers to use `read-state`. A native embedder exposes\n+the equivalent immutable named-field state and explicit snapshot replacement;\n+it need not implement Clojure records, but must preserve their transition\n+semantics. The `yin.vm.engine.host.v1` ABI (§E.3) serializes these snapshots\n+and checked value references. Treat linear memory as a private execution\n+cache. The guest-agnostic synchronization protocol across every host/guest\n+seam is:\n+\n+1. **Public entry / host-to-guest:** `step`, `run`, and restore accept the supplied state map as authoritative. Import the guest's declared machine-state fields (for the register machine's eight-field instance — `:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:store-of`, `:value`, `:halted?`, and `:blocked?` — see [`yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`](./yin.vm.debruijn.register.md) §10.1), plus the current code layout and engine state. W1 imports unconditionally. A later cache may skip only after proving all relevant keys agree with its last materialized snapshot; a retained private token alone is not proof. In particular, externally `assoc`-modified state (such as `(assoc parked :pc 2 :halted? false)`) must execute the requested state. Import a copied or privately owned active state shadow so running an old or externally modified map never mutates another returned map.\n+2. **Guest-to-host:** before every state-consuming `engine/*` call, including `handle-effect`, pinning, collection, scheduler, park/resume and module work, materialize all of the guest's declared execution fields onto the VM record. Materialize them also at every public `step`, `run`, restore or inspection return. Keep the record's protocol implementations so `module/gc-roots` can inspect the current map. Dense memory synchronization without map synchronization is insufficient.\n+3. **Host completion:** the returned host state is the new authority, including its execution fields and every extension key. Apply only the current operation's specified post-service changes to that returned state, then reimport it into memory. Never overlay a pre-service header onto it. In particular, `handle-effect` sets `:value` even for nonblocking effects; preserve that value, resource/heap/GC updates, stores, counters, queues and custody fields. A plain non-tail primitive call, by contrast, only updates the guest's destination/program counter in the kernel and does not automatically set `:value`.\n+4. **Seam site coordinate:** before a host service, the map contains the instruction's absolute site coordinate (`:pc`), unless the source transition explicitly advances it first (such as parking in the FFI path). Capture the boundary payload at the site; apply the operation's coordinate update exactly once after service completion. Mailbox state does not count as a completed guest instruction.\n+\n+This synchronization barrier is also a GC safety requirement: `:cell/new` may\n+collect *inside* `handle-effect`, before the adapter receives its result. At\n+that moment map-based execution fields (`:value` and the guest's active\n+registers/frames/continuation) must already be current. Reuse the engine's\n+exact logical heap tracing rules; arena retention of a host value cannot\n+substitute for marking the heap cells that value references.\n+\n+The program store is logically an immutable map, usually name-keyed but **not\n+restricted to names**: `:store-get`/`:store-put` accept `:data` keys,\n+including keywords and numbers in the corpus. Its linear-memory\ndiff --git a/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md b/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md\nindex 15b3f928b..8088eb1f9 100644\n--- a/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md\n+++ b/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md\n@@ -1204,3 +1204,532 @@ agree. The full register-VM end condition adds a validator-approved kernel\n with both R4 tiers complete, the R3 report published for the owner to read,\n and cross-stream R fetch and verification via the B6 linker. The\n project does not stop at R2: R3's numbers inform, they do not decide.\n+\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 10. Wasm execution instance (2026-10-19, design only)\n+\n+Status: design, owner-authorized planning; not implemented. Sections 1–9 above\n+(as amended on 2026-10-10 and 2026-10-15) remain authoritative for the register\n+image contract and the landed R4 register kernel.\n+\n+> **Amendment 2026-10-19 (design only): WebAssembly execution instance and\n+> K0/W0 register conformance fixtures.**\n+>\n+> Consensus provenance (2026-10-18): gpt-6-astra, author; gemini-4-argon,\n+> reviewer; five review rounds, APPROVE on r5. Author thread:\n+> `01a14f30-ca56-7530-bb93-3a870eca7a7b`; reviewer thread:\n+> `f365ef1d-caa2-4379-8e96-51e64ca36af8`. It does not report an implementation\n+> or runtime acceptance result.\n+>\n+> Owner rulings and decomposition lineage (2026-10-19):\n+> 1. Register-image-to-WebAssembly lowering, the 10-region linear-memory layout,\n+>    and all 23 opcode lowerings live in [`yang.wasm.md`](./yang.wasm.md).\n+> 2. Because the host-independent execution contract belongs to `yin.vm.engine`,\n+>    the service import ABI is named `yin.vm.engine.host.v1` (renamed from\n+>    `yin.register.host.v1` in r5 §4.1.1 by explicit owner ruling on 2026-10-19).\n+>    The guest-agnostic execution-host contract, the canonical\n+>    `yin.vm.engine.host.v1` protocol tables, and the K0/W0 differential\n+>    conformance method live in [`yin.vm.engine.md`](./yin.vm.engine.md)\n+>    (`§E.1–§E.5`).\n+> 3. By explicit owner ruling (2026-10-19), neither `yin.vm.register-wasm.md`\n+>    nor `yin.vm.conformance-kit.md` exists as a separate `yin.vm.*` document:\n+>    the register-machine instance of the WebAssembly execution host and the\n+>    register-specific K0/W0 conformance fixtures and W0–W6 slice gates are\n+>    folded into this section (§10). Normative content is otherwise frozen.\n+> 4. **Precedence over older §5.2 prose in this document:** §5.2.2 above\n+>    (lines 866–878) still shows `:segment` and `:hash` on each return frame;\n+>    `yin.vm.linker.md` §7.3 r6/r7 and current\n+>    `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc` supersede that prose:\n+>    return frames contain `{:site-pc :return-pc :frames :regs :live :dest}`\n+>    plus optional `:store-of`, with no code space, and restore never rewinds\n+>    code space. Likewise §5.2.3 above (lines 911, 953) uses historical\n+>    `:store-updates` wording; current `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc` merges\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
